  "title": "Kidney function effector gene predictions (Sheng et al., 2021)",
  "bodyHtml": "<p>This table displays results from the study:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Mapping the genetic architecture of human traits to cell types in the kidney identifies mechanisms of disease and potential treatments.<br />\r\nSheng X, Guan Y, <i>et al.</i><br />\r\nNat Genet. 2021 Sep;53(9):1322-1333. doi: 10.1038/s41588-021-00909-9..<br />\r\nPMID: <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/34385711\" target=\"_blank\"> 34385711 </a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The genes listed below were prioritized as potential kidney function effectors based on colocalization of genetic association signals for six kidney function traits with cell fraction adjusted eQTLs that were generated from human kidney tubule and glomerular samples. Click the Research Method tab for more details.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This study also prioritized <a href=\"/research.html?pageid=sheng_sbp_191\" target=\"_blank\">genes associated with systolic blood pressure</a>.</p>\r\n",
